    {
      "id": "why-it-matters",
      "title": "Why it matters",
      "body": "These phrases keep the interaction cooperative when repeating the same words is not helping. For \"Please say it slowly\", the useful move is putting the need first and leaving room for the helper to confirm the detail. Pause after the phrase so the person can confirm before you add more words.",
      "presentation": "plain-text"
    },
    {
      "id": "traveler-insight",
      "title": "Traveler insight",
      "body": "In When You Don't Understand, locals often answer with a confirmation, a handoff, a price, or a follow-up question rather than a long explanation. That makes Hãy nói từ từ nhé strongest when you say it once, pause, and let the other person show the next step. If speech still does not land, move to writing, pointing, or showing the exact word on your phone.",
